[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":998},["ShallowReactive",2],{"page-\u002Fvue":3},{"id":4,"title":5,"body":6,"description":991,"extension":992,"meta":993,"navigation":844,"path":994,"seo":995,"stem":996,"__hash__":997},"content\u002Fvue\u002Findex.md","Learn Vue.js — From Zero to Pro",{"type":7,"value":8,"toc":970},"minimark",[9,14,18,23,52,56,92,96,101,255,259,354,358,417,421,507,511,600,604,678,682,686,703,707,717,721,732,736,743,747,806,810,956,960,963,966],[10,11,13],"h1",{"id":12},"learn-vuejs-from-zero-to-pro","💚 Learn Vue.js — From Zero to Pro",[15,16,17],"p",{},"A comprehensive, edge-case-covering Vue 3 curriculum. Each document is self-contained and covers its concept deeply enough that a careful reader can go from beginner to pro Vue developer. The Composition API is treated as the primary style throughout, with the Options API explained alongside it — you'll meet both in real codebases.",[19,20,22],"h2",{"id":21},"how-to-use-this-course","How to Use This Course",[24,25,26,34,40,46],"ol",{},[27,28,29,33],"li",{},[30,31,32],"strong",{},"Read sequentially"," for a structured path (01 → 24).",[27,35,36,39],{},[30,37,38],{},"Jump to a chapter"," as a reference when you hit a concept in the wild.",[27,41,42,45],{},[30,43,44],{},"Build the capstone project"," in chapter 24 after every few chapters, adding features as you learn them.",[27,47,48,51],{},[30,49,50],{},"Keep the official docs and Vue DevTools open"," alongside — reactivity is best understood by poking at it live.",[19,53,55],{"id":54},"prerequisites","Prerequisites",[57,58,59,62,82,85],"ul",{},[27,60,61],{},"Solid HTML & CSS fundamentals.",[27,63,64,65,69,70,73,74,77,78,81],{},"Comfortable JavaScript (ES2015+): ",[66,67,68],"code",{},"let","\u002F",[66,71,72],{},"const",", arrow functions, destructuring, modules, promises\u002F",[66,75,76],{},"async","-",[66,79,80],{},"await",".",[27,83,84],{},"Node.js installed (LTS recommended).",[27,86,87,88,91],{},"A code editor (VS Code + the ",[30,89,90],{},"Vue - Off